WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.893
Before blood flows through a zebrafish brain, its first vessels form.

00:00:04.893 --> 00:00:09.469
Some endothelial cells carry tiny projections called primary cilia.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.919
These images are from the actual published experiments.

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:19.629
Fluorescent zebrafish reveal red endothelial membranes and green ciliary structures.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:29.649
At twenty-four hours after fertilization, cilia cluster around newly forming spaces inside early cerebral vessels, before circulation begins.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.858
These spaces develop into vessel lumens.

00:00:32.858 --> 00:00:38.882
Our moving diagram is an explanation; the microscope images are the experimental evidence.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:46.886
The researchers then disrupted cardiac troponin, stopping embryonic heart contractions and blood flow.

00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:49.319
Would that change cilia distribution?

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:50.967
It did not.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:58.967
Early cilia remained around nascent vessel spaces, indicating that this initial patterning was independent of circulation.

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:04.876
Later in development, hindbrain capillaries sprout, meet and connect.

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:09.095
Cilia appear near those newly developing intravascular spaces.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.461
This branching animation explains those connections.

00:01:13.461 --> 00:01:18.509
It is not recorded microscopy, and it does not reproduce measured growth speeds.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:25.147
When circulation begins, cilia persist in curved and branching vessels.

00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:27.666
Some bend when red blood cells pass.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:39.917
Disrupting intraflagellar transport genes increased intracerebral hemorrhages, indicating that normal ciliary function contributes to vascular integrity.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:45.963
Increased shear stress was associated with premature cilia loss and vessel instability.

00:01:45.963 --> 00:01:49.353
The experiment does not identify every causal step.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:55.467
Primary cilia appear before flow and help stabilize developing cerebral vessels.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:59.565
Their underlying molecular mechanisms remain an open question.
